body: "Raised by CodeRabbit on #84. pm-github's reusable sync and closeout workflows only run an npm script from `npm-project-dir` after the tracker change. pm-rust's callers use `tests/oracle`, which has no scripts, so both post-change scripts are disabled. A closeout PR that closes items therefore ships an unchanged `CHANGELOG.md`, and the dispatched `ci.yml` (`just release-check` → `just changelog-check`) rejects it.\n\nOptions:\n1. Add `\"changelog:full\"` to `tests/oracle/package.json`, delegating to the single source of truth: `just changelog-full` from the repository root. This needs `just` on the runner, so either the reusable workflow installs it, or a node wrapper reproduces the recipe from the justfile constants.\n2. Add an optional pm-github input that installs a named tool (pinned action) before the post-change script.\n\nUntil this is fixed, a closeout PR needs a manual `just changelog-full` push."
